  "notes": "Claimed here on `west-coast-club`'s hand-off. \"The lane's dance-and-R&B hybrid and its most rhythmically adventurous singer\" — and the rhythmic claim is where this model spends: \"Melody is light, agile mid-soprano with very high rhythmic density and syncopation — she phrases across the beat rather than on it\". That is the highest melody `densityPerBar` among the atmospheric half of this section, a low `chordToneBias` so the line does not sit on the chord, and `straightEighthsProb` near zero. The modelled kit is the trap one (clap on 3, triplet hat rolls) at the entry's 128–150 read band; the four-on-the-floor house/garage and 2-step kits are documented in the entry but are not authored as `modes`, because the volume gives them no separate harmonic content and a mood that differs only in feel fails the roster's mood gate. \"Layered electronic percussion (rimshots, reverse hits, vocal chops as percussion) throughout\" is the perc block, which is deliberately wider than the lane norm. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum number, the 808 slide figures and the melody density band; the entry marks its tempo bands `[LOW-CONF]` and its drum patterns as idiom inference. ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research. ⚠ **The countermelody reached 969/1000 distinct answers against a floor of 980 (2026-08-17, counter variety floor), and every other lever this gate has was already clean here** — no empty-bar bias, no one-bar phrase length, and no lead allowed to thin below two notes a bar. What was left was the style pool: `generators::counter` can play five answer shapes and this block asked for 2. `octave_echo` is added at weight 2 because the entry already names it — \"heavily processed synths, chopped and pitched vocal samples used as riffs, and dark pads — plus heavy vocal chopping/pitching as an instrumental layer\" — and a pitched vocal chop used as an instrumental layer is the lead transposed and displaced, which is `octave_echo`. It also makes the authored `echoOffset` of `1/16` mean something: with no echo style in the pool that parameter could never be read. ⚠ The weight is INFERRED; the layer it weights is not.",
